{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:j2s2-certification",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "The array in \\(\\mathrm{def:j2s2-instance}\\), with common interval \\([0,2]\\) and \\(D=2\\), belongs to \\(\\mathcal M\\): its pre laws meet the smooth-density bounds, its same weight spans both pre and post no-intervention quantiles, its observed post laws have at most two atoms, and its pooled Gram satisfies the maintained bound for \\(0<\\lambda\\leq1/375\\). For every \\(\\kappa\\in(0,\\infty)\\), \\(G,R>0\\), and \\(\\varepsilon>0\\), the compactification and interval algorithm of \\(\\mathrm{thm:oracle-common-cutoff}\\) terminates for the certified family \\(\\{\\mathfrak E_{2,2}(h_f,h_c):0\\leq h_f\\leq2G/\\lambda,\\ 0\\leq h_c\\leq2R\\}\\). It returns an interval of width at most \\(\\varepsilon\\) containing \\(\\sup_{0\\leq h_f\\leq2G/\\lambda,\\,0\\leq h_c\\leq2R}Q_{0.95}\\{(1+\\kappa)^{-1}A_t(V_{(\\infty,h_f)})+\\kappa(1+\\kappa)^{-1}\\Psi_t(h_c,Z)\\}\\), and every coverage probability used in the optimization is enclosed between explicit lower and upper Gaussian-cell sums differing by at most \\(\\varepsilon\\). As \\(R\\to\\infty\\) and then \\(\\kappa\\to\\infty\\), the face term vanishes and the certified family reduces to the one-donor Bernoulli problem, where \\(\\widehat w_\\ell=w_\\ell=1\\) and every weight and cross term is zero, reproducing \\(1.913<c_B^*\\leq1.914\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(D\\)",
      "\\(\\mathcal M\\)",
      "\\(\\kappa\\)",
      "\\(G\\)",
      "\\(R\\)",
      "\\(\\varepsilon\\)",
      "\\(\\mathfrak E_{2,2}(h_f,h_c)\\)",
      "\\(h_f\\)",
      "\\(h_c\\)",
      "\\(\\lambda\\)",
      "\\(A_t(V_h)\\)",
      "\\(V_h\\)",
      "\\(t\\)",
      "\\(\\Psi_t(d,Z)\\)",
      "\\(Z_{jtr}\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat w_\\ell\\)",
      "\\(w_\\ell\\)",
      "\\(c_B^*\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:model-class",
      "def:j2s2-instance",
      "thm:face-weight-limit",
      "thm:three-phase-expansion",
      "thm:oracle-common-cutoff",
      "thm:bernoulli-honesty-penalty"
    ],
    "justification": "This finite face-plus-collision instance is the early kill test for the claimed certification machinery and links it to the independently checked Bernoulli bracket.",
    "gap": "No direct DSC inference paper supplies a certified probability enclosure for a simultaneous local simplex face and atomic knot collision.",
    "consumer": "It gives a reproducible validation case before calibration of the intervention-versus-no-intervention QTE is applied to higher-dimensional mosquito-abundance support patterns.",
    "proof_tex": "For \\(a\\in[0,2/5]\\), let \\(Q_a(u)=u+a u(1-u)\\).  Then\n\\[\n Q_a'(u)=1+a(1-2u)\\in[3/5,7/5],\\qquad Q_a''(u)=-2a.\n\\]\nThe induced density satisfies\n\\[\n f_a(Q_a(u))=\\frac1{Q_a'(u)}\\in[5/7,5/3]\\subset[1/2,2],\n \\qquad\n |f_a'(Q_a(u))|=\\frac{2a}{Q_a'(u)^3}\\leq\\frac{100}{27}<4.\n\\]\nThus donor one, donor two, and their treated convex combination satisfy the pre smoothness constants in \\(\\mathrm{def:j2s2\\mbox{-}instance}\\).  Exact span holds in the pre period by construction and in the post period by the definition of \\(Q^N_{0,2,\\ell}\\).  All weights are nonnegative and sum to one under the displayed bounds on \\(h_f\\).  Every observed post law has two atoms and lies in \\([0,2]\\); cell sampling and sample divergence are stipulated in the construction.\n\nFor \\(v=(z,-z)\\in L\\),\n\\[\n v^\\top H_\\ell v=z^2\\int_0^1\n \\left\\{\\frac25u(1-u)\\right\\}^2du\n =\\frac{2z^2}{375}=\\frac1{375}\\|v\\|_2^2.\n\\]\nTherefore the strong Gram assumption holds for every\n\\(0<\\lambda\\leq1/375\\), proving membership in \\(\\mathcal M\\).\n\nFor fixed \\(G,R\\), the nuisance rectangle\n\\(0\\leq h_f\\leq2G/\\lambda\\), \\(0\\leq h_c\\leq2R\\) is compact.  The loss is precisely\n\\[\n (1+\\kappa)^{-1}A_t(V_{(\\infty,h_f)})\n +\\kappa(1+\\kappa)^{-1}\\Psi_t(h_c,Z).\n\\]\nApplying the active-set, endpoint-order, Gaussian-box, interval-grid, and bisection construction proved in\n\\(\\mathrm{thm:oracle\\mbox{-}common\\mbox{-}cutoff}\\) gives a terminating interval of width at most \\(\\varepsilon\\) containing the displayed supremum of \\(0.95\\) quantiles.  The lower and upper cell sums in that proof differ by at most the requested tolerance after refinement, which proves the stated probability enclosure.\n\nFinally, the limiting stable weight is \\((1,0)\\); the donor-two endpoint coefficient is therefore zero.  As \\(\\kappa\\to\\infty\\), the coefficient of the face quadratic tends to zero, uniformly on every Gaussian tail box by the projection bound, while the endpoint coefficient tends to one.  Letting \\(R\\to\\infty\\) first makes \\(h_c\\) range over \\([0,\\infty)\\).  Gaussian tail control then passes these statements to the \\(0.95\\) quantiles.  The remaining loss is exactly the one-donor Bernoulli loss of\n\\(\\mathrm{thm:bernoulli\\mbox{-}honesty\\mbox{-}penalty}\\), so the certified limit reproduces\n \\(1.913<c_B^*\\leq1.914\\).",
